 always a polynomial.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our expressions in turn.\n\n- Expression I is a polynomial. It's a sum of two polynomials, and polynomials are closed under addition.\n\n- Expression II is a polynomial. It's a product of two polynomials, and polynomials are closed under multiplication.\n\n- Expression III is a polynomial. Even though polynomials are *not* closed under division, the quotient of these two polynomials results in a polynomial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{3}-4{x}^{2})÷(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{x({x}^{2}-4x)}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{x}({x}^{2}-4x)}{\\cancel{x}} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-4x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139534858 true] [17592186315435 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315436 13194139534858 true] [17592186315435 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315437 13194139534858 true] [17592186315435 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315438 13194139534858 true] [17592186315435 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315439 13194139534858 true] [17592186315435 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315440 13194139534858 true] [17592186315435 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534858 true] [17592186315435 1041 "selection" 13194139534858 true] [17592186315435 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315436 13194139534858 true] [17592186315435 1110 #uuid "f0fbd1d9-1ff7-5fc6-825d-2de23b2c5361" 13194139534858 true] [17592186315436 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139534858 true] [17592186315436 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534858 true] [17592186315436 1111 #uuid "e16708c3-dece-5d8f-b9a9-d44aa1ae1d91" 13194139534858 true] [17592186315437 1034 "I only" 13194139534858 true] [17592186315437 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534858 true] [17592186315437 1111 #uuid "777ad2ff-bff1-5c4f-ac5b-9608e6509b55" 13194139534858 true] [17592186315438 1034 "III only" 13194139534858 true] [17592186315438 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534858 true] [17592186315438 1111 #uuid "042d5b69-3606-5780-b44c-539f0ee4a926" 13194139534858 true] [17592186315439 1034 "I a